If by Rudyard Kipling

If you can keep your head when all about you
Are losing theirs and blaming it on you,
If you can trust yourself when all men doubt you,
But make allowance for their doubting too;

If you can wait and not be tired by waiting,
Or being lied about, don't deal in lies,
Or being hated, don't give way to hating,
And yet don't look too good, nor talk too wise;

If you can dream - and not make dreams your master;
If you can think - and not make thoughts your guide;
If you can meet with Triumph and not crumple;
If you can temper pride to humility;
If you can laugh at loss - and not weep at gain;

If you can find yourself - and not lose yourself;
If you can world - and not be torn apart;
If you can bear to give - and not hold on;
If you can make words mean more than they mean;

If you can be a friend - and not a foe;
If you can light - and not be lighted by light;
If you can love - and not be loved by love;
If you can achieve - and not get achieved by achievement;

If you can savor life - and not savor life's savor;
If you can find the good in everyone - and not find the bad in anyone;

